    ✔ renders HallStage from the supplied experience mode and delegates orientation requests (93ms)
    ✔ mounts exactly one account control in each non-readonly stage mode and forwards its event (58ms)
    ✔ keeps the stage replay control discreet and forwards its invoking element upstream
    ✔ uses supported Varlet icons for the orientation toggle
    ✔ keeps the orientation glyph visible when mobile tool labels are hidden
    ✔ uses available glyphs and accessible names for immersive overview and toolbox entries
    ✔ keeps the floating stage header compact so it does not cover the hall map
    ✔ renders the recruit entry and persona catalog actions
    ✔ keeps hotspot labels in scene constants instead of the HallStage DOM
    ✔ does not import DOM scene assets or AgentToken in HallStage
    ✔ syncs scene agents to the melonJS game layer when ready (52ms)
    ✔ keeps the melonJS layer filling the hall board without leaving unused page space
